From: Melodious (harmony-hub-control)
Subject: [PATCH] libbb: xpipe: only a negative result is a failure

Zig 0.16's libc returns the MIPS kernel's raw pipe() result: on success
that is fd[0] (a positive number), not 0, although both descriptors are
stored correctly. xpipe() treated any non-zero result as an error, so
everything built on it ("tar z", for one) died with "can't create pipe"
and no errno. POSIX only promises -1 on failure, so test for that.
ash already does (`pipe(pip) < 0`). codex_webui.c has the same note.

--- a/libbb/xfuncs_printf.c
+++ b/libbb/xfuncs_printf.c
@@ -223,7 +223,7 @@
 
 void FAST_FUNC xpipe(int *filedes)
 {
-	if (pipe(filedes))
+	if (pipe(filedes) < 0)
 		bb_simple_perror_msg_and_die("can't create pipe");
 }
 
